.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"All the hairs of the manatee may be vibrissae.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHpim0279.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seehund.jpg/500px-Seehund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seehund.jpg/1280px-Seehund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Seehund.jpg/500px-Seehund.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Macrovibrissae and supraorbital vibrissae of the common harbor seal (Phoca vitulina)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASeehund.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Catyawn.jpg/500px-Catyawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ce/Catyawn.jpg/500px-Catyawn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A yawning cat shows how the mystacial macrovibrissae can be swept forward.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACatyawn.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png/500px-Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png/1280px-Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4c/Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png/500px-Sea-lion_seal_vibrissa.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The upper, smooth whisker belongs to a California sea lion. The lower undulated whisker belongs to a 